      "subject": "Pointwise UCB",
      "result": "complete-scaffold-proof-plan-after-single-local-correction",
      "reason": "Translation continuity in the sup norm gives continuity of actual functions. Conjugation gives translation invariance; the joint-action bound has the correct x0^-1 x order. Haar full support gives sup=essential sup, so means restrict along an isometric injection. No arbitrary representative is evaluated."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Convolution smoothing and associativity",
      "result": "complete-scaffold-proof-plan-after-single-local-correction",
      "reason": "The identity L_g(f*phi)=(L_g f)*phi follows from y=gz; no commuting-right identity remains. Inversion/right translation preserve null sets. The bounded actual convolution has the stated sup norm bound and is continuous by strong L1 translation continuity. Compact-parameter finite partitions prove associativity even with bounded Borel phi, then L1 density extends it. No hidden product-Borel or global sigma-finite Fubini premise is needed."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Topological invariant mean",
      "result": "complete-scaffold-proof-plan-after-single-local-correction",
      "reason": "Compact L1 tails and finite uniform partitions justify m(f*psi)=m(psi) for UCB psi. Applying it to e_U*phi and using the published right L1 approximate identity proves m((f*e_U)*phi)=m(e_U*phi) and the correct convergence estimate. Associativity and independence of the probability kernel give topological invariance; positivity and unitality persist."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Restricted regular representation",
      "result": "complete-scaffold-proof-plan-after-single-local-correction",
      "reason": "The explicit a_x fibers have compact support. Rho covariance gives the exact Delta_H(k)^(1/2) right-regular coefficient, and left Haar invariance makes it descend to xH. Local common compact h-support gives joint continuity; quotient support is compact p((supp f)^-1). Finite Borel partitions approximate uniformly on compact H-sets by positive coefficient sums. J is an involutive unitary intertwiner by Haar inversion, and Cc density plus the coefficient norm bound extends to every L2 vector. No section, direct integral or countability premise is used."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Norm-approximately invariant densities",
      "result": "complete-scaffold-proof-plan-after-single-local-correction",
      "reason": "The prior modular sign was wrong. The one correction now uses f-sharp(y)=f(y^-1)Delta_G(y^-1), so Haar inversion makes it a probability density. Full complex L1 weak testing is supplied by real sigma-finite duality on clopen sigma-compact cosets, summably accurate clipped continuous approximations on compact exhaustions, global continuous gluing, Borel limit, and Cc extension. It avoids a global union-of-null-sets argument. The convolution adjoint identity uses compact partitions and L1 approximation. Mazur applies to the full weak topology of the finite product; its convex combinations preserve probabilities, and the finite norm-net estimate proves compact uniformity."
    },
